{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — It appears that the he was omitted from the word YHWH in 'in the heavens He established His throne,' therefore the bet is opened [dagesh-less]. And the meaning of this verse: 'for I am the servant of HaShem, for I know that His kindness encompasses all.' And the sense: for there is nothing above the heavens, as far as the eye can see. And some say: for the heavens are the source of kindness and the wellspring of faith."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "The 'omitted he' refers to a textual observation about the Masoretic spelling of יהוה in this psalm; 'the bet is opened' means without a dagesh, taken by Ibn Ezra as evidence of an elided he. The quoted phrases 'in the heavens…' and 'for I am the servant of HaShem' are not direct citations of this psalm but appear to reference or paraphrase other verses; their exact referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:49.621585375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}